> I have a magic lamp. Should I try to get a wish from it?
Definitely a worthwhile strategy -- I always bless the first scroll of
genocide I can find and use it on L, just because I've heard how nasty
they can be.  On the other hand, if your god leaves you with most stuff
cursed, you might want to try a blessed scroll of remove curse -- if
you've already seen one then wish for a blessed magic marker and use
that, so you can get multiple scrolls of remove curse.  (Your stuff
will be cursed randomly after grabbing the amulet, too.)
If you wind up wishing for scrolls, wish for 2 or 3 -- you may not get
them all but you'll still get one at least, and if you have an extra
you can use it on mindflayers(h - NOT if you are a dwarf!!!), sea
creatures(;), or whatever happens to be your next imminent death (e.g.
gremlins[g]).

Also, in future you might want to consider keeping gems in main
inventory, or at least one of each kind you have -- just to distract
curses from hitting your really good stuff.

One more thing:  Keep a wand of cancellation handy if you can.  You
probably know this, but in case you don't, *never* put it in your BoH,
or they'll both explode and you lose everything in the BoH.  However,
if your BoH gets cursed, simply drop it, move one square away, and zap
it with wand of cancellation -- that'll cancel the bag's cursedness
(making it uncursed) and won't hurt the stuff inside.

Come to think of it, you could probably break a wand of cancellation to
uncurse everything you have, but that would also have nasty effects
such as blanking all scrolls and spellbooks, completely unenchanting
weapons and armor, and converting potions to water or fruit juice.
Still, if it's the only method you have, you might want to keep that in
mind.



